      "content": "thanks. that's a good start for the framework. i want to get really granular with the hygiene and gathering parameters so the model doesn't over-smooth the data.\n\nspecifically, regarding point 1 and 2: when we look at the 'cultural habits' or 'tendencies' in these districts, are we talking about specific behaviors that are more prevalent in, say, Hispanic or Black communities versus the white-majority district 1? for instance, are there certain types of social/communal gatherings or specific ways of interacting in public spaces that are more characteristic of these groups and would drive higher transmission? i want to be able to assign higher 'risk weights' to those specific cultural behaviors in the simulation if they are statistically more likely to occur in those demographics.",
